  "method": "Weights stay BOD 0.30, eutrophication 0.25, nitrogen risk 0.20, coliform 0.25. rawComposite is the original weighted mean plus multi-layer and thickness bonuses, clamped at 1. underlying keeps the same weights but uses the unclamped organic index bod/10 + cod/30 so measured mg/L values are not flattened. calibratedComposite (also written to composite) rescales underlying across the published hotspots from 0.15 to 1 for display and colour. High is yellow. TSS is not used. Nitrogen and coliform stay classes. BOD and COD numbers are the measured pixel values.",
  "calibration": {
    "reason": "Every published cell reached rawComposite 1.00 because class severities are already 0.7–1.0 and the bonuses are added before the cap.",
    "rawComposite": "min(1, weightedMean + layerBonus + thickBonus)",
    "underlying": "Same weights. BOD term is bod/10 + cod/30 with no dataset-max division and no cap.",
    "rank": "underlying descending, then thickness, then max BOD, then max COD",
    "calibratedComposite": "0.15 + 0.85 * (underlying - min) / (max - min) across the 12 published hotspots",
    "highColour": "#FBC02D"
  },
